# Lemmas of prelude's constructors and functions on the parallel filters.
# A filter is the parallel of a term with a type: the defines filter_nat
# and filter_boolean of parallel_types, for the naturals and for the booleans,
# whose type boolean_type is the choice true + false. The module is compiled with prelude and parallel_types, whose
# names it uses: the modules compiled together are one namespace.
#
# Every lemma here is a theorem of λ-lattice-unit-η (CONTRIBUTING.md,
# "Terms"); each declaration cites its paper proof. None needs induction,
# and none rests on a conjecture. The contracts with no known derivation
# without induction are not here: the own
# contracts of unary and natural_double, typed instead through the typed
# branch of nat_fold (filtered_recursion_naturals.pl), and those of natural_equal,
# natural_at_least and natural_difference (prelude.pl's TODO).

# The constructors pass their filters. true and zero are one term, the
# address of λλ.1, so true_filtered is also filter_boolean @ zero = zero.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "parallel_types") "natural")
λ _ nat_fold filter_nat _
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "prelude") "natural")
λ zero successor unary _ _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "parallel_types") "boolean")
λ _ filter_boolean
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "prelude") "combinators")
λ _ _ compose _ _ _ _
. export
λ _ rewriting _ _
. rewriting
λ _ lemmas _
. lemmas
  # unary is the structural recursion it unfolds to (beta), so it has the
  # typed branch nat_fold_filtered @ zero @ successor, by
  # nat_fold_filtered_branch and nat_fold_filtered_contract of
  # filtered_recursion_naturals.pl, as natural_double has by natural_double_as_fold.
  ( λ s
    . s (λk. k "unary_as_fold") unary (nat_fold zero successor) λ_ md _. md λk. k "[unary_as_fold](docs/design/gezi-set-equations-proofs.md)"
  # A filter after the same filter is redundant.
  + λ s
    . s (λk. k "filter_nat_idempotent") (compose filter_nat filter_nat) filter_nat λ_ md _. md λk. k "[filter_nat_idempotent](docs/design/gezi-set-equations-proofs.md)"
  + λ s
    . s (λk. k "false_filtered") (filter_boolean false) false λ_ md _. md λk. k "[false_filtered](docs/design/gezi-set-equations-proofs.md)"
  + λ s
    . s (λk. k "true_filtered") (filter_boolean true) true λ_ md _. md λk. k "[true_filtered](docs/design/gezi-set-equations-proofs.md)"
  + λ s
    . s (λk. k "zero_filtered") (filter_nat zero) zero λ_ md _. md λk. k "[zero_filtered](docs/design/gezi-set-equations-proofs.md)"
  )
